[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-95983"] :question/problem "Which of the following are third-order ordinary differential equations?\n\n- ${y}^{‴}+3x{y}^{′}=xy$\n- $3{y}^{″}{y}^{′}-2xy=2{y}^{′}$\n- ${x}^{3}{y}^{′}-2x={y}^{″}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of third-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{‴}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a third-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴}.$\n\n- Equation II is not a third-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is not a third-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186262013 :question/answer-fields 17592186262014] {:db/id "q-96669/selection/ma-v1/5f669b830b8629931fca766c99e72078df7d19422cfbdf8963200836911eb045/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "a6903af0-a20c-5e4b-99fd-253aeabbec65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96669/selection/ma-v1/5f669b830b8629931fca766c99e72078df7d19422cfbdf8963200836911eb045/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "1752fc5a-635f-53e4-853c-360095f2087a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96669/selection/ma-v1/5f669b830b8629931fca766c99e72078df7d19422cfbdf8963200836911eb045/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "88b9ed92-1d67-59a0-b022-096ba914be65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-9666