{y}^{‴}+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){y}^{′}={x}^{2}y$\n- $5{y}^{″}{y}^{′}+3xy=4{y}^{′}$\n- ${({y}^{′})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}=y$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation II is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{′}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/answer-fields ["q-96669/selection/ma-v1/5f669b830b8629931fca766c99e72078df7d19422cfbdf8963200836911eb045"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-96662/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "9057c7e4-d0dc-542f-bfc7-2bb5c4a08dea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96662/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "65f0722d-0101-5178-b7dc-b2389fd00257" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96662/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ccaa90e0-e835-5136-bb0b-818379831351" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96662/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "17279daa-0ab3-596b-8cbc-fa602bcff6d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96662/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "8f2b3e1b-d7dd-5cd3-a4d0-6dff4c